WEBVTT

00:18.935 --> 00:22.771
We have seen a star in the east.

00:24.524 --> 00:29.194
It told us the Son of God is born.

01:01.019 --> 01:04.897
NATIVITY PLAY - SERMON - DINNER

01:05.023 --> 01:07.858
The Lord Jesus
was laid in a manger

01:07.984 --> 01:11.653
to bring salvation
to the souls of those

01:11.780 --> 01:14.990
with no place of their own.

01:15.116 --> 01:18.285
Nothing is harder
than to have no place

01:18.411 --> 01:22.498
but many are those without one.

01:22.624 --> 01:23.874
Tell me about it!

01:24.000 --> 01:27.336
In their solitude,
they long for someone who will say:

01:27.462 --> 01:28.837
"I want you to be here."

01:28.963 --> 01:30.422
Not me, thanks.

01:30.548 --> 01:31.882
Be quiet!

01:32.008 --> 01:37.429
Jesus was born to offer those alone
a place in which to be alive!

01:40.350 --> 01:42.726
"Joy to the world,
the food has come."

01:42.852 --> 01:45.395
Gin! It's "the Lord has come"!

01:45.980 --> 01:47.856
You don't know much, do you?

01:47.982 --> 01:50.526
More than some queer.

01:50.652 --> 01:54.029
I am a mistake made by God.

01:54.155 --> 01:56.824
In my heart, I am a woman.

01:56.950 --> 01:58.826
Women can have children.

01:59.327 --> 02:02.830
What if a miracle like
the Virgin Mary getting pregnant

02:02.956 --> 02:05.624
was to happen to a queer?

02:06.126 --> 02:12.297
Better give me a little extra.
After all, I'm eating for two.

02:36.906 --> 02:38.240
Serves you right!

02:41.369 --> 02:42.452
Miyuki!

02:43.830 --> 02:45.706
Time to eat!

02:49.502 --> 02:51.003
Miyuki!

02:51.129 --> 02:54.423
Close your legs!
Act like you were a woman.

02:54.549 --> 02:55.757
I am a woman.

02:55.884 --> 02:58.760
And it's a waste
to spill food like that.

03:00.263 --> 03:02.514
Don't just gobble your bread.

03:02.640 --> 03:07.477
Eat it with love for the people
who made and brought it here.

03:07.604 --> 03:11.899
I hate that Bible-thumping.
You're just like Akiko.

03:12.025 --> 03:13.358
Who's Akiko?

03:15.028 --> 03:16.153
My old lady.

03:16.279 --> 03:17.279
Well!

03:17.405 --> 03:19.239
Don't call your mother that.

03:19.365 --> 03:21.742
Eat shit, you old fart.

03:21.868 --> 03:24.119
"Shit" I'll take, but "fart" I won't!

03:24.245 --> 03:26.079
That hurts! You old...

03:26.789 --> 03:28.457
"bag lady."

03:28.583 --> 03:33.587
You peep pretty loud for a chick
that can't even find its own worms.

03:33.713 --> 03:37.049
Should a burden on society like you
be talking?

03:37.175 --> 03:41.178
You're a burden on us.
What does that make you?

03:42.263 --> 03:44.973
The kettle the pot's calling black!

03:46.559 --> 03:48.185
You mouthy brat!

03:49.062 --> 03:52.564
Can't you at least get along
at Christmas?

03:53.149 --> 03:56.193
Oh, yes.
Miyuki, I got you a present.

03:59.447 --> 04:00.948
They're gone!

04:01.074 --> 04:04.284
A whole set of
"World Literature for Children".

04:04.410 --> 04:06.912
Why would I need that?

04:07.038 --> 04:08.872
Hana looked hard for those!

04:08.998 --> 04:13.001
Even a homeless teenage runaway
needs a Christmas present!

04:14.379 --> 04:16.588
I choose not to go home.

04:16.714 --> 04:20.217
Six months on the street
means you don't have a home.

04:20.343 --> 04:23.220
I can go home any time I want to.

04:23.346 --> 04:26.890
It's the ones who say that
who never do.

04:27.016 --> 04:29.059
Speak for yourself, you old geezer!

04:29.560 --> 04:32.396
What are you doing to Dostoevsky?

04:33.314 --> 04:36.775
I won't take that, today of all days!

04:38.069 --> 04:41.238
Not even my father ever hit me!

04:42.448 --> 04:45.117
So I'll do it for him!

04:48.955 --> 04:51.415
Grow up, will you?

04:52.750 --> 04:53.959
Don't hurt yourselves.

04:54.752 --> 04:56.461
Show more respect, kid!

04:56.587 --> 04:58.130
I'm not a kid!

04:58.256 --> 05:00.841
With little tits like these?

05:00.967 --> 05:03.135
You filthy old pervert!
That's harassment!

05:03.261 --> 05:05.178
Will you two stop?

05:08.349 --> 05:09.224
Huh?

05:28.828 --> 05:30.329
It's been...

05:30.455 --> 05:31.788
...abandoned.

05:32.457 --> 05:34.458
There, there, there.

05:37.211 --> 05:39.338
CARE FOR THIS CHILD.

05:42.091 --> 05:45.260
What a world! Oh, man!

05:45.386 --> 05:49.848
Oh, my! You're a little girl.
I wonder what your name is.

05:49.974 --> 05:51.641
"John Doe."

05:51.768 --> 05:53.935
She's a girl, I said!
He's so rude!

05:54.771 --> 06:00.317
How old was I when I started
living like this? Thirty-something?

06:02.320 --> 06:08.742
I still thought that I was better off
than a child with no home.

06:16.459 --> 06:20.712
There, there, now!
We'll take you somewhere warm.

06:23.174 --> 06:25.425
The cop shop's that way!

06:27.512 --> 06:30.347
This is a Christmas present
from God!

06:30.473 --> 06:33.308
She's our baby!

06:33.434 --> 06:34.643
Huh?

06:45.530 --> 06:49.032
A TOKYO GODFATHERS COMMITTEE
PRODUCTION

06:52.412 --> 06:55.914
DEVELOPED BY MASAO MARUYAMA
ORIGINAL STORY BY SATOSHI KON

06:56.833 --> 07:00.252
SCREENPLAY BY
KEIKO NOBUMOTO & SATOSHI KON

07:02.422 --> 07:05.632
CHARACTER DESIGN:
KENICHI KONISHI & SATOSHI KON

07:05.758 --> 07:09.553
ANIMATION DIRECTOR:
KENICHI KONISHI

07:10.471 --> 07:13.640
ART DIRECTOR: NOBUTAKA IKE
COLOUR DESIGN: SATOSHI HASHIMOTO

07:13.766 --> 07:15.100
CO-DIRECTOR: SHOGO FURUYA

07:15.226 --> 07:17.227
DIRECTOR OF PHOTOGRAPHY:
KATSUTOSHI SUGAI

07:19.147 --> 07:22.607
MUSIC: KEIICHI SUZUKI
SOUND DIRECTOR: MASAFUMI MIMA

07:24.694 --> 07:26.361
Sorry!

07:26.487 --> 07:29.406
What do you mean,
take her with us?

07:29.532 --> 07:32.117
I'm just doing God's will.

07:32.243 --> 07:34.369
Her parents might come back.

07:34.495 --> 07:38.123
What parent would leave
a child out in this cold?

07:38.249 --> 07:40.917
That's a devil, not a parent!

07:43.880 --> 07:47.299
Kiyoko wanted us to find her.

07:47.425 --> 07:48.633
"Kiyoko"?

07:48.759 --> 07:51.261
"Kiyoko"? Why "Kiyoko"?

07:51.721 --> 07:55.599
From kiyo, "pure,"
on this purest of nights.

07:56.225 --> 07:59.478
- How tacky!
- Kiyoko's a fine name!

07:59.604 --> 08:01.980
Did you have
a girlfriend named that?

08:02.106 --> 08:03.732
Idiot!

08:03.858 --> 08:08.695
Look, we can't just name her!
She's not a puppy or a kitten!

08:08.821 --> 08:10.322
So I'm taking her home.

08:10.448 --> 08:11.823
To a cardboard box?

08:11.949 --> 08:13.783
There's no room!

08:13.910 --> 08:18.955
This is a once-in-a-lifetime chance!
Let me feel like a mother!

08:22.084 --> 08:23.710
A haiku:

08:24.295 --> 08:30.634
"A little baby, powdery snow
on its cheeks, on this holy night."

08:30.760 --> 08:34.679
DIRECTED BY SATOSHI KON

08:46.651 --> 08:48.276
Peek-a-boo!

08:50.238 --> 08:52.614
Oh, dear! Tell me what's wrong!

08:52.740 --> 08:54.282
Shut up!

08:58.579 --> 08:59.204
Hey!

08:59.330 --> 09:04.084
I know, I know, he's not your mommy.
He's just a homeless homo.

09:04.210 --> 09:06.878
Don't say that in front of her!

09:07.004 --> 09:10.882
A baby crying around here
will sound weird!

09:11.008 --> 09:14.261
We're going to take you
to the police soon, okay?

09:14.387 --> 09:16.805
You're not going anywhere, are you?

09:16.931 --> 09:19.641
Idiot! We're taking her to the police!

09:19.767 --> 09:21.935
Don't shout or she'll never shut up!

09:22.061 --> 09:25.480
Why won't you stop crying?
Are you hungry?

09:25.606 --> 09:26.606
There, there!

09:26.732 --> 09:29.150
Maybe she's sick.

09:42.915 --> 09:46.585
Tomorrow.
I promise I'll take her then.

09:47.753 --> 09:52.340
Christmas should be
the happiest day of the year.

09:52.466 --> 09:55.844
If we take her in now, it'll always be
the worst day of her life!

09:57.555 --> 10:01.266
Maybe... she needs a diaper.

10:11.277 --> 10:13.194
Hana, boil some water.

10:13.321 --> 10:14.904
I'll make some milk.

10:15.031 --> 10:17.324
Hey! Whose side are you on?

10:17.450 --> 10:22.078
Go buy some water!
My angel isn't drinking from the tap!

10:22.204 --> 10:23.913
Why me?

10:25.374 --> 10:29.919
Where does a bum get off telling me,
"Them that works eats"?

10:31.797 --> 10:36.676
Just for tonight, remember.
Tomorrow we take her to the police.

10:39.055 --> 10:43.058
So "no man is an island"
after all, huh?

10:47.104 --> 10:49.189
You're buying water?

10:50.107 --> 10:52.067
A Christmas miracle.

10:52.610 --> 10:54.694
What a haul!

11:01.285 --> 11:03.578
Watch where you're going, brat!

11:03.704 --> 11:05.914
You watch where you're going!

11:09.001 --> 11:11.586
I was married once.

11:11.712 --> 11:13.505
With a child?

11:13.631 --> 11:17.175
No, don't tell me.
I don't want to hear this!

11:18.719 --> 11:22.055
You never forget for one second.

11:22.181 --> 11:26.601
A child's the only thing
you hold dearer than life itself.

11:28.104 --> 11:29.688
A boy?

11:29.814 --> 11:31.106
No.

11:36.028 --> 11:37.570
Bullshit!

11:37.697 --> 11:39.406
Come on! Give it back!

11:39.532 --> 11:44.035
Hey, you're the girl
who hangs out with Gin.

11:44.161 --> 11:45.829
Get out of here, will you?

11:45.955 --> 11:50.542
- We don't want Gin after us.
- Why not?

11:50.668 --> 11:54.587
You're the light of his life,
that's why not!

11:54.714 --> 11:59.926
There's not much light
in a cardboard box.

12:00.052 --> 12:02.262
Let me have this book.

12:04.890 --> 12:06.850
How old?

12:06.976 --> 12:09.227
Twenty-one, I think.

12:09.687 --> 12:13.898
Five or six years older than Miyuki,
I guess.

12:14.024 --> 12:15.859
That old?

12:15.985 --> 12:18.403
If she was alive.

12:20.030 --> 12:24.951
When I was 20, I got a girl pregnant
and we got married.

12:25.077 --> 12:27.370
I was in heaven.

12:27.496 --> 12:31.374
You could have poked me in the eye
and I'd have just smiled at you.

12:31.500 --> 12:37.547
But my daughter got sick,
and the medical bills were huge.

12:37.673 --> 12:41.926
I was something
of a bicycle racer then.

12:42.928 --> 12:46.431
I needed money.
There was this race...

12:46.557 --> 12:48.183
You threw it?

12:50.436 --> 12:54.314
A punk I knew had this scheme.

12:54.440 --> 13:00.278
They found out, I got kicked out
of racing, and my girl died.

13:00.404 --> 13:03.656
I just didn't feel like working anymore.

13:03.783 --> 13:06.910
And then my wife followed my daughter.

13:07.036 --> 13:08.119
Oh, no!

13:09.538 --> 13:12.207
That's how you get to be a man like me.

13:12.333 --> 13:15.752
I didn't want to hear that.
I hate sad stories!

13:16.962 --> 13:19.088
It's freezing!

13:22.760 --> 13:26.179
- You're used to this.
- Kind of.

13:26.305 --> 13:28.264
I'll give her the milk.

13:29.308 --> 13:31.142
Dreams do come true.

13:31.268 --> 13:36.064
I always dreamed of being
the mother of a little girl.

13:36.190 --> 13:38.525
A nice, warm house, a pretty daughter.

13:38.651 --> 13:41.361
Even if my husband was no good,

13:41.487 --> 13:44.531
I would accept dire poverty
as long as I had my child.

13:44.657 --> 13:46.699
Feed the poor kid!

13:51.705 --> 13:53.581
You're so pretty.

13:54.375 --> 13:58.086
The prettiest little girl in the world.

14:23.445 --> 14:25.154
What do you want?

14:25.281 --> 14:26.573
They're gone.

14:29.785 --> 14:31.995
Santa Claus, maybe?

14:32.121 --> 14:35.290
"Uncle Bag" and the baby are gone.

14:35.416 --> 14:38.167
What's that queer thinking about?

14:40.963 --> 14:43.548
Man, he's got big feet!

14:43.674 --> 14:45.967
You can't have feet fixed.

15:03.068 --> 15:04.944
Are you taking her back?

15:06.363 --> 15:09.032
There's probably an APW out on her.

15:09.158 --> 15:11.659
- And for you.
- I doubt it.

15:12.453 --> 15:15.705
An arrest warrant, maybe.

15:17.082 --> 15:20.376
Her parents are probably
sorry about this now.

15:20.502 --> 15:22.754
So let's take her to the police.

15:23.547 --> 15:27.842
A baby's always better off
with its real mother.

15:27.968 --> 15:29.719
Not necessarily.

15:31.639 --> 15:34.474
Sometimes a foster mother's better.

15:34.600 --> 15:36.935
- What?
- Don't be stupid.

15:37.728 --> 15:40.939
I never knew my real mother.

15:42.942 --> 15:47.570
But I'll bet if she saw me now, she'd flip.

15:48.906 --> 15:51.824
How can someone homeless
raise a child?

15:51.951 --> 15:54.452
I know, I know!

15:55.537 --> 15:59.415
I don't want her shunted
from one foster home to another

15:59.541 --> 16:04.337
without even one memory
of ever having been loved.

16:04.463 --> 16:08.132
You don't have to be a foundling
to feel that.

16:08.258 --> 16:10.593
They must have had their reasons.

16:10.719 --> 16:13.513
Nothing should make you
abandon a child!

16:15.099 --> 16:20.103
That means you've taken love
and tossed it away, like trash.

16:21.563 --> 16:24.524
Yeah, but what can we do about it?

16:25.234 --> 16:26.651
Find her mother.

16:28.904 --> 16:31.948
And ask why she abandoned her baby.

16:33.283 --> 16:35.785
If she can make me understand,

16:36.662 --> 16:39.247
I'll forgive her,
and my mother too.

16:40.082 --> 16:42.291
Find her?

16:42.418 --> 16:44.002
How?

16:48.090 --> 16:50.049
We'll have to pay again.

16:50.634 --> 16:53.928
This is an expensive year-end!

16:54.054 --> 16:56.264
What if we find another baby?

16:56.390 --> 16:58.933
They don't toss them out in twos.

17:10.154 --> 17:12.030
Another key!

17:12.156 --> 17:16.117
Look at these panties.
You'd catch cold in them!

17:16.827 --> 17:19.328
Are they the ones?

17:22.875 --> 17:24.917
Are these your folks?

17:25.419 --> 17:27.211
Look, business cards.

17:34.720 --> 17:38.181
A hostess club won't be open
at this hour.

17:38.640 --> 17:41.059
We've got some walking to do.

17:41.185 --> 17:43.436
You've gotta be kidding!

17:46.732 --> 17:48.608
He was eating for two!

18:01.955 --> 18:07.585
But why pack like you're off on a trip
and then abandon a baby?

18:08.087 --> 18:11.422
Maybe it was one last trip
they were taking.

18:11.548 --> 18:13.925
A family suicide?

18:14.051 --> 18:18.387
Then what do we do?
We can't search the next world.

18:18.514 --> 18:19.972
Shh!

18:26.105 --> 18:29.190
We apologise
for any inconvenience.

18:29.316 --> 18:33.194
Trains will be delayed
due to heavy snowfall.

18:34.655 --> 18:36.239
It's so hot in here!

18:36.365 --> 18:38.074
What a stink!

18:38.575 --> 18:41.619
Have you bathed lately?

18:42.329 --> 18:44.247
No. Or washed my clothes.

18:44.373 --> 18:45.998
How embarrassing!

18:56.093 --> 18:58.052
Oh, dear! There, there.

18:58.178 --> 19:01.597
Did she piss herself?
That's why it stinks.

19:01.723 --> 19:03.558
It's you that stinks!

19:03.684 --> 19:06.686
- Quiet!
- Shut that kid up!

19:21.368 --> 19:23.953
- Watch it!
- Hey!

19:33.672 --> 19:36.465
- Miyuki!
- What's she up to?

19:43.182 --> 19:45.474
We wasted our train fares.

19:46.185 --> 19:48.519
It was me who paid them.

19:50.022 --> 19:53.524
I'm sorry, there's no more milk.

19:53.650 --> 19:56.277
Go ahead, blame it all on me.

19:56.403 --> 19:59.572
Oh, cheer up! Let's sing a song.

20:04.369 --> 20:05.411
What's that?

20:05.537 --> 20:08.289
- The Sound of Music, of course.
- Never heard of it.

20:16.590 --> 20:19.926
That's going to make you even hungrier.

20:29.019 --> 20:30.770
I'm starving!

20:31.438 --> 20:33.397
I told you!

20:33.899 --> 20:36.400
Look after my little angel.

20:37.778 --> 20:39.487
Go on without me.

20:39.613 --> 20:44.242
Just say you'll never forget
the queer you once knew.

20:44.368 --> 20:46.827
Look. A cemetery.

20:46.954 --> 20:48.871
I'm not dead yet!

21:01.802 --> 21:04.679
Now I'm alive again!

21:05.389 --> 21:10.309
But there's nothing for a baby
in these offerings to the dead!

21:10.435 --> 21:12.436
We'll get by!

21:12.896 --> 21:15.606
Yeah, sure. "We'll get by!"

21:15.732 --> 21:19.110
People keep on saying that
till they end up living like us.

21:19.236 --> 21:25.157
And while we keep on saying it,
the kid'll end up under a stone here.

21:25.284 --> 21:27.034
"Kiyoko"! She has a name!

21:27.160 --> 21:31.998
Yeah, whatever. And she's cute.
She's so pretty.

21:32.457 --> 21:35.001
But listen to me. I'm serious.

21:35.585 --> 21:37.044
You listening?

21:37.963 --> 21:41.549
If you really care about that kid,

21:41.675 --> 21:44.802
you'll find her someone
to take care of her.

21:44.928 --> 21:47.430
I speak from experience.

21:47.556 --> 21:49.724
That's what her parents said, I bet.

21:49.850 --> 21:53.644
What do you mean?
I wouldn't abandon a kid.

21:53.770 --> 21:56.063
Don't be stupid!

21:56.189 --> 21:59.150
No. Your family abandoned you!

21:59.735 --> 22:03.237
There you go again!
Am I going to sit and listen

22:03.363 --> 22:06.324
while some dumb queer
pisses on me?

22:06.450 --> 22:10.536
What are we doing here? Tell me.

22:10.662 --> 22:12.538
Wracking our brains!

22:12.664 --> 22:15.958
We're scavenging offerings
left in a cemetery.

22:16.084 --> 22:19.045
And why? Because we're homeless.

22:19.171 --> 22:22.214
- Stop it!
- No! I'm not going to stop.

22:22.341 --> 22:25.301
We are three good-for-nothing bums

22:25.427 --> 22:27.887
who can't even look after ourselves.

22:28.013 --> 22:30.389
Shut up! I'm thinking!

22:30.515 --> 22:32.391
I won't shut up.

22:32.517 --> 22:37.855
You can't get milk from an old queer's
tits, no matter how hard you think.

22:37.981 --> 22:42.234
Come on, Hana!
You know we can't do this.

22:42.361 --> 22:44.195
Speak for yourself!

22:44.321 --> 22:47.281
This way, the whole family will be dead.

22:56.124 --> 22:57.958
Oh, my!

22:59.169 --> 23:01.712
You're so lucky, Kiyoko!

23:01.838 --> 23:03.964
God must really love you!

23:05.008 --> 23:06.509
Then why was she...

23:06.635 --> 23:07.968
...dumped?

23:09.054 --> 23:10.554
Left!

23:10.680 --> 23:14.683
- That's a dead end.
- It's right!

23:17.604 --> 23:19.480
- Tails.
- Heads.

23:28.615 --> 23:31.659
What's this guy doing, parking like that?

23:31.785 --> 23:34.870
Doesn't he know
what a "public thoroughfare" is?

23:55.517 --> 23:57.143
How did that happen?

23:57.269 --> 24:03.232
Bad luck. The car got stuck,
and I forgot the parking brake.

24:03.358 --> 24:05.693
Then someone shouted,
"Dorothy, wait!"

24:05.819 --> 24:11.365
And then I heard, "Whoops!"
and the damn car rolled on top of me.

24:12.951 --> 24:18.956
I don't bring my men with me
when I'm visiting the old man's grave.

24:19.541 --> 24:23.419
I owe you.
Call me if you're ever in trouble.

24:23.545 --> 24:25.796
Oh, no, we never have any trouble.

24:25.922 --> 24:27.965
You're from Kinshicho?

24:28.091 --> 24:30.801
We were just going there.

24:30.927 --> 24:33.304
I know it's rude to ask.

24:33.430 --> 24:35.556
If it's rude, then don't ask.

24:35.682 --> 24:37.141
Come on.

24:38.518 --> 24:41.395
Would you know this establishment?

24:41.521 --> 24:42.897
CLUB SWIRL: "MIDORI"

24:44.065 --> 24:45.733
Know it?

24:46.568 --> 24:50.779
Its owner's marrying my daughter today.

24:52.073 --> 24:56.911
He's one of my men,
but he's too cocky.

24:57.037 --> 24:59.455
I was against it.

24:59.581 --> 25:01.916
But your daughter chose him.

25:02.042 --> 25:05.753
The daughter I brought up,
married to a man like that.

25:07.339 --> 25:08.464
Know what I mean?

25:09.341 --> 25:13.719
But if your daughter's
happy with him,

25:13.845 --> 25:15.763
isn't that the main thing?

25:15.889 --> 25:16.972
You're right!

25:17.098 --> 25:24.230
I went to the old man's grave
so I wouldn't cry at the wedding.

25:24.356 --> 25:25.856
Watch the road!

25:31.821 --> 25:33.322
Good evening, sir!

25:35.367 --> 25:37.284
Make yourselves at home.

25:50.340 --> 25:52.132
Daddy, you're late!

25:52.259 --> 25:56.178
Sorry, sorry. I almost got killed.

25:56.304 --> 25:59.056
I owe them my life.

25:59.182 --> 26:00.724
My daughter, Kiyoko.

26:00.850 --> 26:02.101
Oh. Hello.

26:12.696 --> 26:15.614
What have you gotten us into?

26:15.740 --> 26:17.992
Just shut up and eat!

26:21.663 --> 26:24.415
Diaper change. Your turn, Miyuki.

26:32.757 --> 26:37.094
Don't you think
Kiyoko has amazing luck?

26:39.598 --> 26:40.639
Yeah.

26:41.349 --> 26:43.309
Maybe she does.

26:46.813 --> 26:49.481
Oh, yeah. Her name's Sachiko.

26:50.025 --> 26:51.358
Not "Midori"?

26:51.484 --> 26:53.068
Just at the club.

26:53.194 --> 26:56.030
She's Sachiko, "happy child,"
though she didn't look it.

26:56.156 --> 27:01.160
But some plastic surgery turned her
into a good little earner.

27:02.829 --> 27:05.623
She quit.
Said she was pregnant.

27:05.749 --> 27:07.625
Do you know where she is?

27:08.501 --> 27:11.003
I doubt you'll wring
any money out of her.

27:11.755 --> 27:14.548
No, I have something to give her.

27:18.386 --> 27:22.097
I'm sorry I spilled your food.

27:22.223 --> 27:25.476
You remember her?
Midori, the skinny broad.

27:27.354 --> 27:29.521
She said her husband was in debt.

27:29.648 --> 27:31.774
What's wrong with you?

27:31.900 --> 27:33.233
That bastard.

27:33.360 --> 27:35.569
Do you know him?

27:36.112 --> 27:38.155
Then she borrowed
more money from us,

27:38.281 --> 27:41.492
and ended up screwed both ways.

27:41.618 --> 27:43.577
You know where she is?

27:44.454 --> 27:47.956
If it weren't for his damn
get-rich-quick scheme,

27:48.083 --> 27:50.918
I'd still be with my wife and kid!

27:51.044 --> 27:53.671
But aren't they both dead?

27:53.797 --> 27:55.923
I'll kill the bastard!

27:56.966 --> 27:59.134
You'll get killed!

28:25.870 --> 28:27.287
Mitsuo! Mitsuo!

28:27.414 --> 28:29.707
It was that maid!

28:29.833 --> 28:31.709
Are you okay?

28:32.794 --> 28:34.169
She's got a gun!

28:35.797 --> 28:36.839
Hey, what?

28:41.886 --> 28:43.679
Kiyoko! Miyuki!

28:44.848 --> 28:45.806
Hey!

29:07.746 --> 29:10.581
Thank you very much.

29:11.416 --> 29:13.792
She's got a gun, you know!

29:13.918 --> 29:17.421
- Our lives are already wasted!
- Hana!

29:22.802 --> 29:23.761
There!

29:49.412 --> 29:53.749
Yes! One of your cabs picked up
a young woman with a baby.

29:53.875 --> 29:56.794
Number 12-25. Send it to...

29:57.962 --> 30:00.881
...the Tokyo Tower.
My name is...

30:03.343 --> 30:06.053
Hey! Wait a minute.

30:10.183 --> 30:15.062
We're homeless bums,
not action-movie heroes.

30:15.522 --> 30:17.523
What we need now is the police.

30:18.566 --> 30:23.570
If you like the police so much,
get them to adopt you!

30:23.696 --> 30:26.448
Those children are like family!

30:26.574 --> 30:28.742
I thought I could depend on you!

30:28.868 --> 30:32.246
Don't talk like you were my damn wife.

30:34.582 --> 30:36.208
I'm not going anywhere.

30:36.334 --> 30:37.459
Gin!

30:37.919 --> 30:40.128
We've done all we could.

30:40.255 --> 30:41.380
You're giving up?

30:42.423 --> 30:45.217
There's nothing we can do.

30:45.760 --> 30:48.470
You really are the lowest of the low!

30:48.596 --> 30:51.765
The best thing you'll ever do
is die in the gutter!

30:51.891 --> 30:55.686
Oh, poor you!
You'll be dead and no one'll care!

30:55.812 --> 30:58.689
All you ever do is cause people trouble!

30:58.815 --> 31:01.441
Dead or alive, you're living trash!

31:01.568 --> 31:04.278
The king of trash!

31:08.491 --> 31:12.828
Okay, so I'm trash. But you're ugly.

31:28.595 --> 31:32.347
- Yes?
- I want to get rid of some trash.

31:37.687 --> 31:40.105
I don't think I'd fit.

31:40.940 --> 31:45.861
Yeah, that's what I am, living trash!

31:47.447 --> 31:51.742
Who cares if you die in the gutter?

31:52.952 --> 31:56.580
You're dead all the same.

32:18.770 --> 32:20.729
You okay?

32:21.522 --> 32:23.899
Hang in there, Gramps.

32:26.319 --> 32:29.696
- May I make one last request?
- What?

32:31.491 --> 32:33.700
Give me a drink of that.

33:24.460 --> 33:27.045
You're not selling me into slavery!

33:29.048 --> 33:31.216
Somebody, help!

33:45.440 --> 33:49.609
I always wanted to die drunk,
in a nice old house.

33:49.736 --> 33:52.904
Now I'm halfway there.

33:53.031 --> 33:55.157
Fate works in strange ways.

33:56.159 --> 33:58.994
I've lived a long time,

33:59.120 --> 34:02.914
but I'm just trash,
as worthless dead as alive.

34:03.041 --> 34:05.167
Don't talk like that!

34:06.002 --> 34:10.172
You remind me of myself
when I was younger.

34:10.757 --> 34:13.467
Looking at you now,

34:13.593 --> 34:16.720
may I make a last request?

34:17.430 --> 34:20.474
Get rid of this for me.

34:20.600 --> 34:26.313
Some people will be hurt
if it's known who I am.

34:26.439 --> 34:30.067
Okay. I understand.
No one will ever know.

34:43.998 --> 34:48.293
Take care of yourself, okay?
May I make a last...?

34:49.087 --> 34:50.253
Request?

34:56.010 --> 34:58.720
And now, goodbye.

35:14.070 --> 35:15.112
That's it!

35:18.282 --> 35:20.075
Thanks, Gramps!

35:25.873 --> 35:28.542
Time for the New Year's clean-up!

35:37.051 --> 35:38.802
Big breasts... Cool!

35:52.525 --> 35:54.025
Husband?

36:09.000 --> 36:12.085
Father... Police.

36:12.211 --> 36:14.171
Your dad's a cop?

36:14.297 --> 36:17.507
- My father was a policeman!
- Father, policeman?

36:20.136 --> 36:25.390
Except I'm the one
he's going to be arresting.

36:40.448 --> 36:41.656
Hold it.

36:44.994 --> 36:47.287
Hi! How've you been?

36:49.916 --> 36:51.917
Now? Just cleaning up.

36:52.043 --> 36:54.211
Hey, wake up!

36:54.337 --> 36:55.420
Come on!

36:58.925 --> 37:00.759
No! Not that!

37:02.178 --> 37:03.929
Time to die, old man!

37:04.055 --> 37:07.015
Kiyo's coming? I'm there!

37:07.725 --> 37:10.143
The girls are drinking near here.

37:10.269 --> 37:11.811
Yeah?

37:13.231 --> 37:15.232
All cleaned up.

37:19.612 --> 37:21.112
Give it back!

37:22.156 --> 37:24.115
Give me that back!

37:25.826 --> 37:30.538
Her foreigner husband looked like
he was in a real bad mood.

37:31.290 --> 37:32.582
Did he hit her?

37:32.708 --> 37:36.086
No, she was being real nice
for a girl so young.

37:36.212 --> 37:39.422
My wife could learn something!

37:40.258 --> 37:43.635
His foreign assailant fled, taking
a young woman and a baby hostage.

37:43.761 --> 37:49.140
With the groom in serious condition,
police speculate this may be a war

37:49.267 --> 37:51.476
between crime syndicates.

37:51.936 --> 37:54.688
Hey, this is serious!

37:54.814 --> 37:56.773
I'm not kidding around, either!

38:03.406 --> 38:05.573
My mum's religious.

38:05.700 --> 38:07.867
She chants all the time.

38:13.791 --> 38:14.874
Me.

38:19.213 --> 38:21.339
Isn't she cute?

38:21.465 --> 38:24.718
I found her. Those spots
on her back look like wings.

38:24.844 --> 38:27.470
So I called her "Angel".

38:28.306 --> 38:30.515
But she's gone.

38:33.602 --> 38:34.811
Father.

38:45.031 --> 38:47.365
I stabbed my father.

38:47.491 --> 38:49.868
I can never go back.

39:16.228 --> 39:19.064
The baby? A gift from God.

39:21.192 --> 39:25.320
Give me a break.
I've got a family at home.

39:25.446 --> 39:27.822
Those children are my family!

39:29.992 --> 39:31.701
They went in there.

39:32.328 --> 39:34.746
- Hey! The fare!
- I'll be right back.

39:34.872 --> 39:37.165
Miyuki! Kiyoko!

39:38.542 --> 39:40.543
Miyuki! Kiyoko!

39:40.669 --> 39:42.337
Where are you?

39:49.553 --> 39:52.430
Kiyoko! Miyuki!

40:09.198 --> 40:11.574
How could you do this to me?

40:13.119 --> 40:14.536
It's your own fault!

40:15.371 --> 40:18.498
You never listen to anything I say!

40:18.624 --> 40:22.669
Use the scarf I made you
to mop up the blood!

40:22.795 --> 40:24.254
What have you done with Angel?

40:24.380 --> 40:27.048
Where is she? Where is my Angel?

40:27.716 --> 40:30.844
She's right here. Our angel.

40:33.139 --> 40:36.433
I'm hungry.
Make me some food.

40:37.685 --> 40:41.479
Why? What are you doing
in my house?

40:41.605 --> 40:45.817
Miyuki, take Kiyoko. I'll get dinner.

40:56.162 --> 41:00.957
Kiyoko! Miyuki!

41:06.046 --> 41:07.338
Uncle Bag?

41:11.177 --> 41:14.762
Oh, I've missed you, my little angel!

41:18.517 --> 41:22.270
I wish I was her mother,
but I'm just another queer.

41:23.606 --> 41:27.775
Miyuki...
I'm so glad you're safe.

41:37.119 --> 41:38.912
Where's the geezer?

41:39.038 --> 41:41.456
He could be dead, for all I care!

41:44.043 --> 41:46.586
I'm dying.

41:56.430 --> 41:58.848
Maybe he went home.

41:58.974 --> 42:00.475
Who cares?

42:00.601 --> 42:02.894
All he thinks about is himself.

42:04.313 --> 42:09.150
Yeah, Miss Hana, but you're in love
with him, aren't you?

42:09.276 --> 42:13.196
Don't be silly!
I like my men to be more "manly".

42:13.322 --> 42:18.826
The kind of man I like is slender,
middle-aged, tanned,

42:18.953 --> 42:22.539
with a divine square-back haircut
and a lower-town accent

42:22.665 --> 42:25.708
who says, "Ah, what the hell,"

42:25.834 --> 42:29.003
when I don't quite have the cab fare.

42:32.341 --> 42:34.801
So, what now, Miss Hana?

42:34.927 --> 42:39.222
Why are you calling me that?
"Uncle Bag" is fine.

42:39.348 --> 42:41.516
It's hard to say.

42:48.566 --> 42:50.024
I'm glad.

42:53.070 --> 42:54.237
He just died there?

42:54.363 --> 42:55.822
He was homeless.

42:55.948 --> 42:57.407
I might be next.

42:57.533 --> 42:58.783
Just do your job.

42:58.909 --> 43:00.952
Gin!

43:03.664 --> 43:06.040
Gin! Gin!

43:06.750 --> 43:08.334
Take it easy.

43:08.460 --> 43:09.460
Gin!

43:09.587 --> 43:11.087
Calm down!

43:19.638 --> 43:23.349
Where is that man of mine?

43:24.476 --> 43:29.063
Kiyo...

43:30.107 --> 43:34.777
If only tonight...

43:36.155 --> 43:40.366
I wanted to see you before I died.

43:42.995 --> 43:45.622
Kiyoko!

44:01.305 --> 44:05.016
What is your desire?
My magic, or an ambulance?

44:05.976 --> 44:09.020
- An ambulance.
- Well! Aren't you rude?

44:10.230 --> 44:14.525
What are we going to do?
Kiyoko can't sleep out on the street!

44:14.652 --> 44:18.863
The geezer's not here,
we're freezing, sleepy, hungry.

44:18.989 --> 44:20.490
This sucks!

44:21.158 --> 44:23.826
I guess there's no choice.

44:29.583 --> 44:32.085
I never thought I'd be here again.

44:38.384 --> 44:42.720
I'm sorry. We're closed
for a private party tonight...

44:44.890 --> 44:46.474
Hana?

44:46.600 --> 44:50.645
I know I have no right
to come strolling in now,

44:50.771 --> 44:54.649
but there's no one else
I can call on, "Mother"!

44:59.279 --> 45:00.905
Hana!

45:01.615 --> 45:02.949
Mother!

45:03.075 --> 45:04.409
Hana!

45:12.126 --> 45:13.084
Geezer?

45:16.422 --> 45:18.256
What happened, Gin?

45:20.676 --> 45:23.261
Some kids beat me up.

45:24.221 --> 45:27.098
I guess I'm just not an action hero.

45:31.395 --> 45:34.063
He said he knew you.

45:34.189 --> 45:37.442
But he said he was homeless,
you know.

45:38.485 --> 45:39.902
So am I.

45:40.028 --> 45:43.740
What? But why?

45:44.950 --> 45:47.243
Since Ken died, I'm like a canary

45:47.369 --> 45:49.996
that's forgotten its song.

45:50.122 --> 45:52.415
You sing all the time!

45:54.251 --> 45:55.668
Isn't she cute?

45:55.794 --> 45:57.628
I wish I could have one!

46:02.760 --> 46:06.262
So Ken died, did he?

46:08.265 --> 46:09.682
AIDS?

46:10.142 --> 46:12.393
He slipped on the soap.

46:12.519 --> 46:16.481
Well, death is always
a hair's breadth away.

46:17.065 --> 46:21.110
But if you were in trouble,
why didn't you come back?

46:23.906 --> 46:27.283
We certainly had fun here, didn't we?

46:29.077 --> 46:31.704
In this old bar

46:31.830 --> 46:35.333
I've had so much to drink

46:36.251 --> 46:38.336
My old memories

46:39.004 --> 46:43.466
All start to blur

46:43.592 --> 46:46.010
My lover

46:46.136 --> 46:49.472
Has left me

46:50.766 --> 46:55.978
People call me notorious

46:56.104 --> 46:57.939
Aw, you're ugly!

46:58.440 --> 47:00.942
Good for nothing

47:01.068 --> 47:01.943
Get off!

47:02.069 --> 47:04.737
Good for nothing

47:05.739 --> 47:09.492
What a terrible thing to say

47:09.618 --> 47:12.078
Eat shit, you old fart!

47:13.705 --> 47:17.625
"Shit" I'll take, but "fart" I won't!

47:24.800 --> 47:28.261
I couldn't come back after I'd done that.

47:28.387 --> 47:32.306
A little bit of money took care of that.

47:32.432 --> 47:35.142
I'm just happy you're all right.

47:37.187 --> 47:40.398
Stop it!
You scare me when you start crying.

47:42.401 --> 47:46.612
What about that baby?
ls the girl its mother?

47:46.738 --> 47:47.989
Well...

47:51.451 --> 47:54.912
Where is your mother, anyway?

47:55.956 --> 47:57.164
Abandoned?

47:57.291 --> 48:00.710
Yes! I've been abandoned!

48:03.213 --> 48:05.840
Them's the breaks, I guess.

48:07.593 --> 48:10.219
I could see me in her.

48:10.345 --> 48:14.557
Born on the street,
and back there again.

48:15.017 --> 48:20.730
That's why I want to find her
a home full of love!

48:20.856 --> 48:25.276
All I ever wanted was love!

48:32.409 --> 48:33.284
Ow!

48:39.958 --> 48:41.834
What the hell?

48:44.463 --> 48:47.006
The geezer's come out.

48:47.132 --> 48:48.507
Where are my clothes?

48:58.310 --> 49:00.144
Way to go, Gin!

49:01.980 --> 49:04.148
Come back any time.

49:05.275 --> 49:07.693
Thank you, Mother.

49:10.781 --> 49:17.286
My mother's white breath as she watches me
set out on a long journey.

50:33.113 --> 50:35.823
Oh, man!

50:35.949 --> 50:39.452
An empty building's always nice,
but look who got here first.

50:43.040 --> 50:46.584
I'd just love to fill up on some meat!

50:47.169 --> 50:49.045
Don't you dare!

50:50.714 --> 50:53.174
Just kidding!

50:57.888 --> 51:01.432
The snow's let up.
Miyuki, will you go shopping?

51:01.558 --> 51:02.600
Okay.

51:02.726 --> 51:04.935
Get me some sake.

51:05.562 --> 51:07.271
Just one.

51:25.290 --> 51:27.625
- No!
- I wish.

51:44.810 --> 51:46.185
"Honey, I'm home."

52:04.121 --> 52:10.126
You stayed in there?
You'd think you were homeless!

52:14.589 --> 52:17.925
Actually, we're looking for these people.

52:19.427 --> 52:21.679
Sachiko Nishizawa.

52:22.139 --> 52:23.389
Do you know her?

52:23.890 --> 52:27.643
She never paid me back for
her Neighbourhood Association dues.

52:27.769 --> 52:30.146
Are you a relative?

52:30.272 --> 52:35.109
No! We're acquaintances of a relative.

52:35.235 --> 52:37.444
Her husband was no better.

52:37.571 --> 52:42.074
Gambling day and night,
and mean when he drank.

52:44.119 --> 52:47.288
Living on his wife's earnings
and borrowed money.

52:47.414 --> 52:49.206
Where are they now?

52:49.332 --> 52:53.002
I wouldn't know.
Mrs Kurumizawa might.

52:53.503 --> 52:56.714
They left about three months ago.

52:57.716 --> 53:04.471
The house was seized for debt.
One night they just up and went.

53:05.265 --> 53:08.517
They were a nice couple at first,

53:08.643 --> 53:12.605
but it wasn't long
before they started fighting.

53:12.731 --> 53:14.773
That's poverty for you.

53:14.900 --> 53:19.153
All that debt didn't stop him
from lording it over her.

53:19.279 --> 53:22.907
Even the most dedicated wife
has her limits.

53:24.034 --> 53:26.118
You'd see bruises sometimes.

53:26.244 --> 53:28.078
The poor woman.

53:28.205 --> 53:30.581
Not on her, on him!

53:30.707 --> 53:31.957
Oh, dear!

53:32.834 --> 53:39.590
But his mother would always
take his side against her.

53:40.675 --> 53:43.510
His parents built them this house.

53:43.637 --> 53:47.598
- Where do they live?
- Mrs Yamanouchi might know.

53:49.935 --> 53:52.311
Her mother-in-law
was always complaining

53:52.437 --> 53:54.647
that she never did any housework.

53:54.773 --> 53:57.024
But her son was perfect, of course.

53:57.150 --> 53:59.902
Of course! That's why I told her

54:00.028 --> 54:04.073
she'd never see a grandchild
with his wife working in a club.

54:04.616 --> 54:07.534
But she did get pregnant.

54:07.661 --> 54:09.912
Well, a man and a woman...

54:10.038 --> 54:13.999
They can always find time
to do what they must!

54:14.125 --> 54:17.086
SHINKOCHO 1-2-25,
MAISON HAPPINESS, APT. 203

54:18.838 --> 54:21.215
What if they ran out
from this new place too?

54:21.341 --> 54:23.842
What a horrible man!

54:23.969 --> 54:29.306
Poor Sachiko! Working to pay off
her husband's gambling debts!

54:29.432 --> 54:30.849
Right.

54:30.976 --> 54:35.688
But I never thought
of abandoning the kid.

54:35.814 --> 54:38.023
- Huh?
- Nothing.

54:38.149 --> 54:42.319
That's no reason to just dump the kid.

54:42.445 --> 54:44.071
I've said that all along.

54:47.242 --> 54:51.620
MIYUKI: ANGEL HAS COME HOME.
DAD.

54:56.126 --> 54:59.044
Doesn't it ever get tired of snowing?

55:01.589 --> 55:03.424
Thank you.

55:13.101 --> 55:16.562
I wonder how we look to them.

55:16.688 --> 55:19.356
Like a bum, a queer,
a runaway and a foundling.

55:19.899 --> 55:23.319
Kiyoko is God's messenger.
We're her servants.

55:24.529 --> 55:27.031
Unpaid servants.

55:27.157 --> 55:30.326
Paying for a father's sins.

55:30.452 --> 55:33.787
Yeah, if her father had been
any good at all,

55:33.913 --> 55:36.206
we wouldn't be going through all this.

55:37.917 --> 55:43.047
Even a good-for-nothing father
never forgets a child.

55:45.091 --> 55:46.925
I'm going out.

55:51.056 --> 55:53.807
What's the matter with her?

55:53.933 --> 55:57.353
A child never forgets its parents.

56:02.108 --> 56:08.989
I never stop wanting
to see my daughter, just once.

56:09.115 --> 56:11.408
So she's alive?

56:11.534 --> 56:12.785
Yeah.

56:12.911 --> 56:14.078
And your wife?

56:15.330 --> 56:20.167
I'm sure she's remarried
and living happily.

56:25.465 --> 56:28.717
Hello. It's me, Miyuki.

56:29.469 --> 56:31.553
Why did you split up?

56:31.679 --> 56:33.764
- Drinking and gambling.
- What?

56:35.016 --> 56:36.350
Just like...

56:37.435 --> 56:39.728
I'm a louse.

56:40.855 --> 56:46.110
But I've always wanted to do
something for her as a father,

56:46.236 --> 56:48.320
even just a little.

56:48.446 --> 56:52.533
When I was gambling,
this would have been nothing.

56:52.659 --> 56:56.245
Now I've had to sweat blood
just to save 30,000 yen.

56:56.371 --> 56:58.789
That's great, Gin!

56:58.915 --> 57:02.209
- We can stuff ourselves!
- Stuff you!

57:11.803 --> 57:13.220
Ishida speaking.

57:22.063 --> 57:25.149
Miyuki? Is that you?

57:27.318 --> 57:29.319
Are you all right?

57:34.701 --> 57:36.160
I'm sorry!

57:36.286 --> 57:37.953
I'm sorry!

57:38.538 --> 57:40.330
I'm sorry!

57:42.584 --> 57:45.085
Excuse me,
but if you wouldn't mind.

57:45.211 --> 57:47.087
"Get out," you mean?

57:47.213 --> 57:50.883
Other customers might like to sit down.

57:51.009 --> 57:54.219
- There's hardly anyone here...
- You guys stink!

57:54.971 --> 57:58.557
What are you?
Homeless or something?

58:03.813 --> 58:05.981
Who are you looking at?

58:08.026 --> 58:09.443
Hold it, you!

58:14.324 --> 58:18.619
Hold it, I said, you low-life!

58:24.125 --> 58:27.836
It's New Year's Sale time
at The Food Store!

58:27.962 --> 58:34.384
Come to The Food Store
for all your special New Year's needs!

58:34.511 --> 58:37.221
See in the New Year with your family!

58:37.347 --> 58:39.139
Call an ambulance, quick.

58:39.891 --> 58:41.308
Right!

58:44.479 --> 58:49.191
I knew it! Kiyoko really is
the messenger of God!

58:51.819 --> 58:53.737
- Hey!
- Miss Hana!

58:53.863 --> 58:55.280
Hey!

58:55.406 --> 58:56.448
Hana!

59:12.715 --> 59:15.467
Following a recent gangland
shooting incident,

59:15.593 --> 59:21.181
police are seeking a fugitive
thought to be Latin American.

59:21.808 --> 59:24.560
Mitsuo Hiruta, shot three times,

59:24.686 --> 59:28.730
in protecting the leader
of his syndicate,

59:28.856 --> 59:34.069
will be questioned
after he recovers from his wounds.

59:34.988 --> 59:38.657
Isn't she cute!
When was she born?

59:38.783 --> 59:41.994
Not long ago, I guess.

59:42.120 --> 59:43.704
So the mother...?

59:43.830 --> 59:45.372
I'm not.

59:45.957 --> 59:48.375
- What's her name?
- Kiyoko.

59:48.501 --> 59:52.421
That's my name too.
What a coincidence.

59:55.091 --> 59:57.509
Your friend is very weak.

59:57.635 --> 01:00:00.554
Make sure he gets rest
and proper nutrition.

01:00:00.680 --> 01:00:01.930
Doctor!

01:00:02.807 --> 01:00:05.309
Believe it or not, we're homeless.

01:00:05.435 --> 01:00:07.644
I'm just a doctor.

01:00:09.063 --> 01:00:14.610
Rest and nutrition don't fit
with our lifestyle, you realise.

01:00:15.570 --> 01:00:21.742
I can try to cure disease.
Lifestyle is something you have to fix.

01:00:21.868 --> 01:00:25.120
All anyone can do is their best.

01:00:27.540 --> 01:00:29.291
Take care.

01:00:32.879 --> 01:00:36.048
The bill for today is 29,830 yen.

01:00:36.174 --> 01:00:40.385
Bring your health-insurance card
and you'll get a refund.

01:00:41.554 --> 01:00:44.014
I'm sorry, Gin!

01:00:44.766 --> 01:00:48.352
Stop crying!
You'll get the bills all wet.

01:00:49.062 --> 01:00:51.063
That's 30,000 yen.

01:01:07.330 --> 01:01:08.664
Kiyoko?

01:01:13.711 --> 01:01:14.753
Dad?

01:01:37.694 --> 01:01:39.778
So you took up nursing.

01:01:41.114 --> 01:01:43.281
I see.

01:01:45.702 --> 01:01:47.619
I'm glad you're well.

01:01:47.745 --> 01:01:53.208
Oh, yeah, I'm just great.
How's your mother?

01:01:53.334 --> 01:01:54.584
Fine.

01:01:55.503 --> 01:01:57.671
Yeah? That's good.

01:01:58.256 --> 01:02:00.006
What are you doing now?

01:02:00.133 --> 01:02:06.430
I'm in recycling.
I had to drop something off here.

01:02:10.476 --> 01:02:12.185
You must hate me.

01:02:13.771 --> 01:02:18.024
I was never
any kind of a father to you.

01:02:18.151 --> 01:02:24.072
But that 30,000 yen was money
I'd saved up for you.

01:02:25.575 --> 01:02:27.075
You may not believe it.

01:02:30.455 --> 01:02:33.749
I always wanted to see you.

01:02:35.042 --> 01:02:39.337
When I was little,
Mum and I searched for you.

01:02:39.464 --> 01:02:42.090
We even checked unidentified corpses.

01:02:43.050 --> 01:02:47.429
After you disappeared,
Mum ran the store herself.

01:02:48.681 --> 01:02:49.473
The store?

01:02:49.599 --> 01:02:53.769
It was hard for a woman
to run a bicycle shop alone.

01:02:54.771 --> 01:02:57.898
That's not quite the same
as a bicycle racer.

01:02:58.024 --> 01:03:04.196
The man you owed money to was shot
and wounded the other day, you know.

01:03:04.322 --> 01:03:05.781
He lived?

01:03:06.824 --> 01:03:08.867
That's a relief.

01:03:08.993 --> 01:03:10.994
I thought you'd say that.

01:03:13.873 --> 01:03:18.794
I ran up the debts, not him.

01:03:20.421 --> 01:03:24.966
Thank that doctor for me.
He seems like a nice guy.

01:03:25.885 --> 01:03:28.303
I'm getting married.

01:03:30.181 --> 01:03:31.932
Oh? That's good.

01:03:32.058 --> 01:03:33.350
To him.

01:03:33.476 --> 01:03:37.938
Great! But isn't he about my age?

01:03:38.564 --> 01:03:42.317
He's been married.
His daughter got sick and died,

01:03:42.902 --> 01:03:45.153
and his wife followed her.

01:03:50.409 --> 01:03:52.244
That man makes me so mad!

01:03:52.370 --> 01:03:53.995
Aren't you moved?

01:03:54.914 --> 01:03:58.834
- Here's the address and phone number.
- Yours?

01:03:58.960 --> 01:04:01.419
The old house is gone.

01:04:01.546 --> 01:04:03.922
Even if you can't now,
call me sometime.

01:04:05.091 --> 01:04:07.467
Kiyoko!

01:04:09.512 --> 01:04:13.640
I've had about all I can stand!

01:04:13.766 --> 01:04:17.435
- Miss Hana?
- Telling us you were a racer!

01:04:18.437 --> 01:04:20.480
I was always at the track.

01:04:20.606 --> 01:04:21.982
Yeah, betting!

01:04:22.108 --> 01:04:26.444
And your debts snowballed
so you couldn't face your family

01:04:26.571 --> 01:04:28.488
and you ran and hid in a cardboard box!

01:04:28.614 --> 01:04:30.365
Yes, damn it!

01:04:30.491 --> 01:04:32.993
That's what your father is!

01:04:33.452 --> 01:04:37.163
He can't bet, he's spineless,
his feet stink and he can't drink!

01:04:37.290 --> 01:04:41.167
He kills off his wife and daughter
to buy sympathy!

01:04:41.294 --> 01:04:44.170
He said you had an incurable disease!

01:04:44.297 --> 01:04:49.718
With a father like that,
you have my sympathy!

01:04:49.844 --> 01:04:53.054
Is this how you repay me?

01:04:53.180 --> 01:04:54.931
Repay you?

01:04:55.057 --> 01:04:57.058
Am I hearing right?

01:04:57.184 --> 01:04:59.394
If we're talking about debt,
I'm waiting for my change!

01:04:59.520 --> 01:05:02.063
Debt's a concept
you don't even understand!

01:05:02.189 --> 01:05:05.775
You understand how to troll
through garbage cans!

01:05:05.902 --> 01:05:08.778
And how to get in debt
and how to make babies.

01:05:08.905 --> 01:05:12.449
Though you're not too good
at raising them, are you?

01:05:12.575 --> 01:05:15.577
And your debts
you shove off on your wife.

01:05:15.703 --> 01:05:19.080
Always running away,
never doing anything right!

01:05:19.206 --> 01:05:22.000
Running away's
the only racing you ever did!

01:05:22.126 --> 01:05:25.170
Miyuki! We're leaving!

01:05:28.090 --> 01:05:29.382
Miss Hana?

01:05:34.764 --> 01:05:36.765
I guess he's better.

01:05:38.100 --> 01:05:41.144
Should you have said that
in front of her?

01:05:43.940 --> 01:05:47.233
If she's his daughter,
she'll forgive him.

01:05:50.154 --> 01:05:53.448
Being able to speak freely

01:05:53.574 --> 01:05:56.409
is the lifeblood of love.

01:05:57.453 --> 01:05:59.412
Maybe I'm naive.

01:06:01.874 --> 01:06:04.209
So you're in love with him?

01:06:04.335 --> 01:06:07.879
Don't be silly.
I'm the Weeping Red Devil.

01:06:08.005 --> 01:06:12.050
- What?
- It's a story I love.

01:06:12.718 --> 01:06:17.555
There was a red devil who wanted
to be friends with people.

01:06:18.516 --> 01:06:23.269
But since he was a devil,
no one would go near him.

01:06:23.396 --> 01:06:27.107
So his friend the blue devil
made a plan.

01:06:28.192 --> 01:06:33.697
He'd wreak havoc among the people,
and the red devil would save them.

01:06:38.828 --> 01:06:40.662
WHEN YOU TRY
TO ACHIEVE SOMETHING,

01:06:40.788 --> 01:06:42.497
SOMEONE'S BOUND TO GET HURT.

01:06:43.541 --> 01:06:46.167
YOU ALWAYS HAVE
TO SACRIFICE SOMETHING.

01:06:46.752 --> 01:06:48.962
The plan worked.

01:06:49.088 --> 01:06:53.967
But the blue devil had to go away,
so they'd never know it was a trick.

01:06:56.804 --> 01:06:58.471
It's a sad story.

01:06:58.597 --> 01:07:02.767
But that means you leave.
Where will you go?

01:07:03.644 --> 01:07:07.022
It's best for everyone
when they're with their family.

01:07:07.148 --> 01:07:09.190
Soon we'll find Kiyoko's mother.

01:07:09.316 --> 01:07:13.653
And then what?
You don't have a real family!

01:07:23.706 --> 01:07:27.042
RARE "LINE OF ONES"
WINS LOTTERY

01:07:27.168 --> 01:07:31.838
Numbers have been drawn for
the annual New Year's Jumbo Lottery.

01:07:32.381 --> 01:07:35.800
Top prize in the 200-million-yen
lottery is a very rare number.

01:07:36.552 --> 01:07:40.805
Group 11, number 111,111

01:07:40.931 --> 01:07:43.600
is worth 50 million yen.

01:07:44.268 --> 01:07:45.560
A different group pays
100,000 yen.

01:07:46.687 --> 01:07:50.065
To repeat,
the winning prize number is...

01:07:51.901 --> 01:07:53.526
This just in.

01:07:54.028 --> 01:07:57.614
Police have released a sketch
of an infant taken

01:07:57.740 --> 01:08:01.409
from a hospital
in Tokyo's Shinagawa Ward.

01:08:03.954 --> 01:08:08.958
We've come all the way here,
but we don't have her address!

01:08:09.085 --> 01:08:11.669
The geezer's got it! Let's go back.

01:08:11.796 --> 01:08:14.130
Where are you going?

01:08:15.716 --> 01:08:19.928
- The police!
- What? You hated that idea!

01:08:20.846 --> 01:08:22.806
I was just ego-tripping.

01:08:23.557 --> 01:08:26.851
Now I want to apologise
to her parents.

01:08:26.977 --> 01:08:31.356
They might not be able to sleep
waiting for news about her.

01:08:31.482 --> 01:08:35.193
That's what we said
from the very start!

01:08:35.319 --> 01:08:39.489
They might even be
about to commit suicide!

01:08:39.615 --> 01:08:43.034
I've done something
that can't be taken back!

01:08:43.160 --> 01:08:45.912
I'll throw myself in this river.

01:08:46.038 --> 01:08:50.208
I'll step neatly out of my shoes,
stand on the handrail, and be at peace.

01:08:50.334 --> 01:08:53.419
But then I'll see a baby's face
on the water.

01:08:53.546 --> 01:08:58.299
No! While I see this child's face,
I cannot die!

01:08:58.425 --> 01:09:00.260
Hey, you!

01:09:00.386 --> 01:09:01.594
No!

01:09:03.931 --> 01:09:07.350
- You're too young for this!
- Please! Let me die!

01:09:14.984 --> 01:09:16.526
You!

01:09:17.319 --> 01:09:19.445
Sachiko Nishizawa...

01:09:22.867 --> 01:09:24.868
What were you thinking of?

01:09:24.994 --> 01:09:27.036
Is that an apology?

01:09:27.163 --> 01:09:31.416
If we hadn't found this child,
she would've frozen to death!

01:09:31.542 --> 01:09:32.876
It wasn't me!

01:09:33.002 --> 01:09:36.171
My husband took her away
when I wasn't there!

01:09:37.381 --> 01:09:40.175
I've looked and looked!

01:09:47.391 --> 01:09:48.975
Is that true?

01:09:51.729 --> 01:09:56.941
All I've suffered
on account of that man!

01:10:08.204 --> 01:10:11.080
"Hi, Mum!"

01:10:19.089 --> 01:10:22.926
God really loves this child, you know.

01:10:23.052 --> 01:10:26.512
I want you to give her lots of love too.

01:10:26.639 --> 01:10:29.599
Do right by her, or you'll pay for it.

01:10:29.725 --> 01:10:31.643
I'm so sorry!

01:10:31.769 --> 01:10:33.019
I'm sorry!

01:10:43.030 --> 01:10:44.906
Mrs Nishizawa!

01:11:31.203 --> 01:11:34.872
What are you doing in here?
Get out of here! Get out!

01:11:35.416 --> 01:11:37.458
Wait! I'm no thief.

01:11:37.584 --> 01:11:39.961
You're lying! Get out!

01:11:40.087 --> 01:11:42.005
Where's the baby?

01:11:44.758 --> 01:11:47.969
Did an old queer and a girl come
to give it back?

01:11:48.095 --> 01:11:49.679
What are you talking about?

01:11:49.805 --> 01:11:51.931
You abandoned a baby!

01:11:54.143 --> 01:11:56.227
I can prove it.

01:11:56.687 --> 01:11:58.855
Are you a cop?

01:11:58.981 --> 01:12:03.568
Huh? I'm just a bum
who was passing by.

01:12:04.778 --> 01:12:06.863
Are you right in the head?

01:12:06.989 --> 01:12:09.324
I'm damn near crazy from all this!

01:12:09.450 --> 01:12:14.704
Why is the baby you abandoned
on the news as being "taken away"?

01:12:14.830 --> 01:12:17.248
They'll call us kidnappers!

01:12:17.833 --> 01:12:21.919
It wasn't me. That's not my kid.

01:12:24.173 --> 01:12:25.381
What?

01:12:27.259 --> 01:12:29.510
There, there! Don't cry!

01:12:29.636 --> 01:12:30.720
Take care.

01:12:31.430 --> 01:12:33.097
Raise her right.

01:12:33.223 --> 01:12:35.308
See you again someday.

01:12:36.935 --> 01:12:39.562
Never leave her again.

01:13:02.503 --> 01:13:10.009
On the year's last day, when all
of a life's accounts have been settled up

01:13:20.187 --> 01:13:24.941
Sachiko stole that baby
out of the hospital.

01:13:25.067 --> 01:13:29.445
She stole a baby
and then abandoned it?

01:13:29.571 --> 01:13:31.531
That's a person's life!

01:13:31.657 --> 01:13:34.283
She lied to me about it!

01:13:34.410 --> 01:13:37.954
And now it's got way out of control.

01:13:38.080 --> 01:13:42.583
I don't want anything to do with it!
Take the kid to the police!

01:13:42.709 --> 01:13:44.127
What?

01:13:45.212 --> 01:13:48.089
Don't act like you're not part of this!

01:13:48.215 --> 01:13:51.676
You don't want to get involved?
You're her husband!

01:13:51.802 --> 01:13:56.055
That's all over!
I'm getting my life back together.

01:13:56.181 --> 01:13:56.973
Look!

01:13:57.099 --> 01:14:00.893
I won 100,000 yen in the lottery.
My luck's turned!

01:14:04.440 --> 01:14:10.653
I know a guy just like you.
He threw away his life and his family.

01:14:10.779 --> 01:14:13.030
No. They threw him away.

01:14:13.157 --> 01:14:15.158
I'm no loser!

01:14:20.080 --> 01:14:22.248
These were in your wife's bag.

01:14:24.668 --> 01:14:28.045
Any idea where she might have gone?

01:14:28.172 --> 01:14:31.716
She said she was going
to be with her baby.

01:14:31.842 --> 01:14:34.635
She was going to kill herself!

01:14:36.513 --> 01:14:38.181
There's no time to waste!

01:14:38.307 --> 01:14:41.893
No! She was just going
to go look for the kid.

01:14:42.019 --> 01:14:44.479
She's desperate.
That only means one thing!

01:14:46.190 --> 01:14:47.648
But where do I look?

01:15:03.874 --> 01:15:04.916
Hana!

01:15:05.042 --> 01:15:06.334
Miyuki!

01:15:08.045 --> 01:15:09.378
Kiyoko!

01:15:15.677 --> 01:15:18.304
God must be busy at this time of year.

01:15:18.430 --> 01:15:20.723
Better once a year than never.

01:15:21.642 --> 01:15:22.350
Geezer?

01:15:31.985 --> 01:15:35.988
You're too late.
You just missed a very moving finale.

01:15:36.114 --> 01:15:38.074
What's the matter?

01:15:41.828 --> 01:15:43.162
"Kiyoko"!

01:15:46.291 --> 01:15:47.667
"Stomach"?

01:15:49.545 --> 01:15:51.128
"Mother"!

01:15:51.255 --> 01:15:54.173
Now that's settled,
what the hell do you mean?

01:15:54.675 --> 01:15:58.553
Fake! The mother! Sachiko's a fake!

01:16:00.764 --> 01:16:02.139
Pardon?

01:16:07.437 --> 01:16:10.022
Why won't you drink?

01:16:10.732 --> 01:16:15.194
A baby has to drink
from its mother's breast.

01:16:15.862 --> 01:16:19.949
We'll never be close if you don't!

01:16:26.373 --> 01:16:28.082
Sorry. Wrong people.

01:16:30.627 --> 01:16:32.587
She can't be far!

01:16:33.046 --> 01:16:35.006
But where do we look?

01:16:35.132 --> 01:16:37.758
We can't just give her up now!

01:16:50.731 --> 01:16:52.231
That's Kiyoko!

01:16:59.448 --> 01:17:01.073
Should you be running?

01:17:01.199 --> 01:17:03.951
If I don't run now, when will I?

01:17:04.077 --> 01:17:04.994
This way!

01:17:19.301 --> 01:17:23.262
Returning stolen goods to a thief!
How could we be so dumb?

01:17:23.388 --> 01:17:25.181
Who said "family suicide"?

01:17:25.307 --> 01:17:26.766
You did!

01:17:32.939 --> 01:17:33.939
- Which way?
- Left.

01:17:34.066 --> 01:17:36.067
- Okay, right!
- Why?

01:17:36.568 --> 01:17:37.902
You're a lousy gambler!

01:17:38.028 --> 01:17:40.112
You got that right.

01:17:40.238 --> 01:17:42.114
Somebody help!

01:17:55.796 --> 01:17:57.046
Hey!

01:17:57.547 --> 01:17:58.506
Wait!

01:17:58.632 --> 01:18:00.341
Thief! Thief!

01:18:00.467 --> 01:18:04.845
- What's wrong?
- A woman just stole my truck!

01:18:05.555 --> 01:18:06.847
Hey! Thief!

01:18:06.973 --> 01:18:09.100
Yes! That woman!

01:18:09.601 --> 01:18:12.395
She's a baby thief!

01:18:26.910 --> 01:18:30.204
Be quiet, will you?
Please! Be a good baby!

01:18:38.630 --> 01:18:40.881
Stop! Give Kiyoko back!

01:18:45.470 --> 01:18:47.179
Give me a break!

01:18:47.305 --> 01:18:49.348
I'm forever in your debt!

01:18:54.563 --> 01:18:55.855
Gin!

01:18:57.274 --> 01:18:59.400
That woman's crazy!

01:18:59.985 --> 01:19:00.860
Get closer!

01:19:00.986 --> 01:19:01.819
I can't!

01:19:01.945 --> 01:19:04.280
You have to, for Kiyoko!

01:19:04.406 --> 01:19:06.282
- Who's Kiyoko?
- Step on it like a man!

01:19:06.408 --> 01:19:07.533
Okay!

01:19:12.414 --> 01:19:15.040
Please! Be quiet!

01:19:18.754 --> 01:19:20.254
- Gin!
- Geezer?

01:19:23.759 --> 01:19:24.800
Geezer!

01:19:24.926 --> 01:19:28.262
Go for it, Gin!
No action star can touch you!

01:19:28.388 --> 01:19:29.889
Pass her!

01:19:30.015 --> 01:19:31.891
- We'll die!
- Step on it!

01:19:32.017 --> 01:19:33.559
Okay!

01:19:35.312 --> 01:19:37.021
Stop crying!

01:19:37.898 --> 01:19:40.983
Don't be afraid.
I'll never leave you again.

01:19:41.485 --> 01:19:42.526
You want to die?

01:19:51.787 --> 01:19:53.704
Gin!

01:20:05.759 --> 01:20:07.009
Gin!

01:20:09.596 --> 01:20:10.638
There!

01:20:12.349 --> 01:20:13.974
- Are you okay?
- Where's Kiyoko?

01:20:14.100 --> 01:20:15.684
- Faster!
- Okay!

01:20:35.372 --> 01:20:35.913
Which way?

01:21:23.253 --> 01:21:25.004
We're at the scene

01:21:25.130 --> 01:21:29.717
where a truck has crashed
into a building in Shinagawa.

01:21:29.843 --> 01:21:34.096
Now a woman holding a baby
has appeared on the roof.

01:21:34.598 --> 01:21:39.393
Witnesses say the woman
is connected with the incident

01:21:39.519 --> 01:21:41.770
as she was driving the truck.

01:21:48.069 --> 01:21:50.863
Now there's someone else on the roof!

01:21:55.535 --> 01:21:56.452
Stay away!

01:21:56.578 --> 01:21:58.787
No!

01:22:05.629 --> 01:22:08.088
Tell me why you took that baby.

01:22:08.214 --> 01:22:11.717
I didn't! This baby is mine!

01:22:11.843 --> 01:22:15.471
You're lying! Its real parents
are worried sick about it!

01:22:15.597 --> 01:22:16.805
That's not true!

01:22:16.932 --> 01:22:20.851
You of all people should know
what it's like to lose a child!

01:22:32.364 --> 01:22:37.618
She's dead. My baby died
before she was even born!

01:22:44.918 --> 01:22:48.712
All the other babies looked
so healthy there in the ward.

01:22:48.838 --> 01:22:51.382
I wanted to die.

01:22:51.508 --> 01:22:54.134
But then this baby smiled at me.

01:22:54.260 --> 01:22:56.387
I decided she was mine.

01:22:56.513 --> 01:23:00.641
I thought as long as I had her,
everything would be fine.

01:23:00.767 --> 01:23:04.478
My husband would mend his ways,
and we'd be a real family.

01:23:04.604 --> 01:23:06.647
That's bullshit!

01:23:06.773 --> 01:23:12.069
Build a family by ruining a baby's life?
If you're going to die, do it alone!

01:23:12.195 --> 01:23:17.032
A life is a life. It's only born once.
You, me, or Kiyoko.

01:23:22.622 --> 01:23:24.665
Give her back, okay?

01:23:32.007 --> 01:23:33.924
I want to be reborn.

01:23:34.926 --> 01:23:37.011
Sachiko!

01:23:38.263 --> 01:23:41.306
Sachiko, don't die!
Come back to me!

01:23:41.433 --> 01:23:45.310
I was wrong!
Please, don't kill yourself!

01:23:45.437 --> 01:23:49.940
We'll start again!
We'll be reborn! Sachiko!

01:23:50.442 --> 01:23:53.235
I'll go first and wait for you.

01:23:57.532 --> 01:23:58.782
Sachiko!

01:24:01.202 --> 01:24:02.536
Please! Let me die!

01:24:02.662 --> 01:24:05.748
Kiyoko wants to see her mum and dad!

01:24:11.713 --> 01:24:13.130
I want to go home.

01:24:16.468 --> 01:24:18.469
I'm sorry!

01:24:26.478 --> 01:24:30.647
Take her to her mother and father.

01:24:40.116 --> 01:24:41.742
Oh, no.

01:24:41.868 --> 01:24:43.202
Hana!

01:24:44.913 --> 01:24:48.082
I'm okay! I'm still alive!

01:25:28.623 --> 01:25:32.668
Inspector, I don't know how to thank you.

01:25:32.794 --> 01:25:36.463
We're not the ones you should thank.

01:25:38.633 --> 01:25:43.679
Man, that was a good sleep!
Get me a cigarette, Miyuki.

01:25:43.805 --> 01:25:46.098
- In my jacket.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:25:46.224 --> 01:25:49.476
That was some New Year's!

01:25:50.311 --> 01:25:52.146
It's "No Smoking" here.

01:25:52.272 --> 01:25:55.440
Lighten up. I'm a hero.

01:25:55.567 --> 01:25:57.693
You mean "we"!

01:26:01.156 --> 01:26:06.535
I guess we won't have to listen
to Kiyoko's damn crying anymore.

01:26:06.661 --> 01:26:08.912
She's not "Kiyoko" anymore.

01:26:09.038 --> 01:26:11.331
I'm not pleased.

01:26:12.250 --> 01:26:14.126
What can we do?

01:26:14.252 --> 01:26:15.919
Not that.

01:26:16.462 --> 01:26:18.630
This is a men's ward.

01:26:21.467 --> 01:26:23.093
Perhaps we're intruding.

01:26:23.219 --> 01:26:25.429
No, it's just...

01:26:25.972 --> 01:26:28.432
I'm told they're homeless.

01:26:28.558 --> 01:26:29.850
Who cares?

01:26:29.976 --> 01:26:32.853
We'd like them to be her godfathers.

01:26:34.647 --> 01:26:35.939
Come in.

01:26:36.858 --> 01:26:37.900
Excuse us.

01:26:38.651 --> 01:26:42.112
The baby's parents
would like to thank you...

01:26:47.785 --> 01:26:49.119
Dad...
